# Local web API. Production / preview builds use https://arsalandev.studio (see eas.json).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://arsalandev.studio

# Google sign-in (optional). Create OAuth clients in Google Cloud Console.
#
# Recommended for Expo AuthSession (id_token → POST /api/auth/google):
# 1) OAuth consent screen
#    - User type: External
#    - Publishing status Testing → add YOUR Google account under Test users
#      (AccessBlocked almost always means Testing + email not listed)
#    - Or publish the app (may require Google verification for sensitive scopes)
# 2) Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID → Web application
#    - Authorized JavaScript origins: https://arsalandev.studio (web Auth.js)
#    - Authorized redirect URIs (add ALL that apply):
#        https://arsalandev.studio/api/auth/callback/google   (web Auth.js)
#        arsalanstudio://oauthredirect                       (native scheme from app.json)
#    - Copy Client ID → EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID and server AUTH_GOOGLE_ID
# 3) Optional native clients (better than Expo Go):
#    - iOS: bundle ID studio.arsalan.app → EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID
#    - Android: package studio.arsalan.app (+ SHA-1) → EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID
# 4) Prefer a Dev Client / EAS build. Expo Go uses host.exp.Exponent redirects and
#    often fails AccessBlocked / redirect mismatch with custom schemes.
#
# Server must accept the same audience via AUTH_GOOGLE_ID (and optional
# AUTH_GOOGLE_IOS_ID / AUTH_GOOGLE_ANDROID_ID / AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS).
# Deploy web branch feat/mobile-google-auth (POST /api/auth/google) before testing mobile.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
